{"name":"Pie in the Sky","hex":"#b0c4f9","fetched":"2026-10-23","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pie in the sky","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fanciful notion; an unrealistic or ludicrous concept; the illusory promise of a desired outcome that is unlikely to happen."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of pie-in-the-sky."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pie_in_the_sky"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pie in the Sky (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Pie in the Sky is a British police comedy drama starring Richard Griffiths and Maggie Steed, created by Andrew Payne and first broadcast in five series on BBC1 between 13 March 1994 and 17 August 1997, as well as being syndicated on other channels in other countries."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Pie_In_the_Sky_Cover_Art.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie_in_the_Sky_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q3440393"},{"title":"Pie in the Sky (1964 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Pie in the Sky is a 1964 American film drama written and directed by Allen Baron and starring Lee Grant, Sylvia Miles, and youngster Richard Bray. Although filmed in 1962, financial and distribution problems delayed release until 1964. Shortly after the initial release, it was retitled Terror in the City."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/65/Terror_in_the_City-filmposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie_in_the_Sky_(1964_film)","wikidata":"Q7191337"},{"title":"Pie","blocks":[{"text":"A pie is a baked dish which is usually made of a pastry dough casing that contains a filling of various sweet or savoury ingredients. Sweet pies may be filled with fruit, nuts, fruit preserves, brown sugar, sweetened vegetables, or with thicker fillings based on eggs and dairy. Savoury pies may be filled with meat, eggs and cheese, or a mixture of meat and vegetables."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg/330px-Top_down_view_of_peach_pie_%28722379748%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pie","wikidata":"Q13360264"},{"title":"Sky","blocks":[{"text":"The sky is an unobstructed view upward from the surface of the Earth. It includes the atmosphere and outer space. It may also be considered a place between the ground and outer space, thus distinct from outer space."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg/330px-July_night_sky_%2835972569256%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sky","wikidata":"Q527"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Pie_In_the_Sky_Cover_Art.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8e/Pie_In_the_Sky_Cover_Art.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APie_In_the_Sky_Cover_Art.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/AlexisSoyerPic.jpg/500px-AlexisSoyerPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/AlexisSoyerPic.jpg/1280px-AlexisSoyerPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/AlexisSoyerPic.jpg/500px-AlexisSoyerPic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Crabbe's portrait of Alexis Soyer that hung on the wall in his kitchen.[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlexisSoyerPic.jpg"},{